cff-version: 1.2.0
title: San Diego Heat Risk Explorer
message: >-
  If you use this tool, its methodology, or its derived data, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  # TODO: add co-authors (PI, SDRCC collaborators) and ORCIDs before minting the DOI.
  - given-names: Connor
    family-names: Mack
    email: cjmack@ucsd.edu
    affiliation: Scripps Institution of Oceanography, UC San Diego
    # orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/cccia-sio/socal-heat-hub'
url: 'https://cccia-sio.github.io/socal-heat-hub/'
abstract: >-
  An interactive, browser-based composite heat-risk viewer for every census
  tract in San Diego County. Users select the variables that matter to them
  across three pillars — heat exposure, population sensitivity, and adaptive
  capacity — and the tool combines them via PCA into a neighborhood-level risk
  map, with LOCA2-downscaled climate scenarios for mid-century and
  end-of-century warming.
keywords:
  - extreme heat
  - heat vulnerability
  - climate adaptation
  - environmental justice
  - San Diego
  - census tract
  - principal component analysis
license: MIT
license-url: 'https://github.com/cccia-sio/socal-heat-hub/blob/main/LICENSE'
# The MIT license covers the CODE only. The data and derived content are CC BY
# 4.0, and embedded third-party data (HPI, UCLA Heat Maps) keeps its own terms.
# See DATA_LICENSE.md, which spells out what the MIT grant does not cover.

